jobs.description:
Within Quinten Health, you will support evidence and data-driven insights generation for optimal decision making and maximal business, medical or public health impact, through the following tasks:
Operating on the framing of the project and participate in the translation of customer needs into data issues;
Participating in the design and implementation of the solution to be provided: data structuring, modeling, interpretation of the results;
Participating in exchanges with the client as well as in the realization of the supports and deliverables of the project;
Participating in scientific and technological watch.
Preferred experience
Coming from an engineering school and / or holding a master's degree in data science, you are looking for an internship and ideally have a 1st experience on a data science project (internships, study projects, ...). You have the following skills:
Python programming;
Good knowledge of statistical and machine learning techniques;
Good knowledge of machine learning libraries for Datascience (e.g., pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, XGBoost, SHAP...);
You are really interested in the Healthcare sector;
You have synthesis and communication skills allowing you to argue technological choices and explain their risks and benefits;
You have qualities of organization and rigor, and the taste for teamwork.
Additional Skills
Knowledge of continuous integration (Git versioning, unit tests);
Knowledge of distributed computing (parallelization and/or Spark);
R programming;
1st experience in Healthcare sector would be a plus.
Quinten Health recruits based on skills, qualifications, and motivation. All applications are considered fairly and evaluated on an equal basis. If you require any accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know

We are building a high-performance ADAS Online team focused on advancing state-of-the-art machine learning and AI algorithms for scene understanding and environmental awareness.
As a machine learning applied scientist, you will contribute to the development and improvement of models within the in-vehicle spatial awareness stack. Work hands-on across data, experimentation, and evaluation pipelines, and grow your ability to tackle increasingly complex engineering challenges in a fast-moving team.
This spatial awareness stack will leverage modern transformer and end-to-end architectures to transform vehicle sensor data along with real-time 3D map data from the cloud into a 3D, semantically defined environment identifying all static and dynamic objects.
What You’ll Do
Develop a solid understanding of the team's physical AI roadmap and contribute ideas that improve algorithms within your area of ownership;
Implement and improve ML / vision transformer models for 3D awareness;
Produce instance detections and segmentation masks, instance tracking, and occupancy modelling;
Contribute to multi-modal fusion pipelines (camera, LiDAR, RADAR), building and validating components against defined requirements;
Apply Transformer-based and representation learning techniques within established frameworks, building confidence in large-scale model development;
Run experiments and benchmarks with guidance, producing clear results and contributing to the team's evaluation practices;
Participate in translating research into production, learning what makes ML solutions reliable and scalable;
Actively seek feedback from senior engineers and apply it to continuously improve the quality of your work.
What You'll Need
3+ years of experience in machine learning, vision transformers, diffusion, or co

Als Data Analist / BI Specialist zorg jij ervoor dat organisaties hun data omzetten in waardevolle inzichten. Je analyseert complexe datasets, vertaalt deze naar heldere rapportages en dashboards en adviseert stakeholders over datagedreven beslissingen. Met moderne BI-tools zoals Power BI, Tableau of Qlik maak je informatie toegankelijk en begrijpelijk. Daarmee help je onze klanten – zoals de Belastingdienst, Gemeente Den Haag, Centraal Justitieel Incassobureau en VGZ – om hun beleid en processen te verbeteren en toekomstgericht te sturen.
Waarom past deze vacature bij jou?
Je hebt een passie voor data en ziet het als jouw missie om cijfers en informatie te vertalen naar verhalen die impact maken. Je bent analytisch sterk, communicatief vaardig en kunt schakelen tussen business en techniek. Je vindt het leuk om samen te werken met collega’s en stakeholders en voelt je thuis in een omgeving waar data centraal staat.
Wat kan je van ons verwachten?
Bij CIMSOLUTIONS krijg je de kans om te werken aan uitdagende en innovatieve data- en BI-projecten bij toonaangevende organisaties. Wij investeren in jouw ontwikkeling en bieden naast een inspirerende werkomgeving:
Een vast dienstverband voor onbepaalde tijd, een max. salaris van € 6.000, bonusregeling, leaseauto, pensioenregeling en maandelijkse onkostenvergoeding;
Opdrachtkeuzevrijheid: Jij bepaalt in overleg waar je aan werkt, met de begeleiding van een personal coach;
Per jaar € 5.000,- opleidingsbudget en daarnaast ook nog eens 5-10 dagen studietijd;
Kennissessies met vakgenoten en inhoudelijke events;
Minimaal 25 vakantiedagen, met de mogelijkheid om extra dagen op te bouwen of te verkopen;
Sociale events zoals sportdagen, weekend weg en gezellige borrels;
Een vestiging bij jou in de buurt.
Persoonlijke ontwikkeling
Bij CI

